{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring","text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First fit in index order (the lexicographically first proper colouring of all) when it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already optimal. Otherwise each vertex in turn takes the least colour its prefix still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extends with (k-colouring’s self-reduction to its decision problem): a Kempe swap of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last colouring found when one avoids the prefix, else DSatur branch and bound over the parts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after the prefix that the vertex touches (on sparse components with conflict-directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backjumping and restarts). Khuller and Vazirani show the lexicographically first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"four-colouring of a planar graph is NP-hard to find, though some four-colouring is found in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"polynomial time. It can be far slower than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":", and its time grows steeply"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with n even on sparse 3-colourable graphs. The search does not check for task cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"ColoringModule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactColoring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/ExactColoring.swift#L625"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE029lexicographicallyFirstMinimumC0AD0C0VyxGyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"ColoringModule","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/Coloring":{"title":"Coloring","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/colorin